# ==============================================================================
# Git Credentials for Claude Flow CI/CD Container
# ==============================================================================
# This file stores Git credentials for HTTPS authentication
# Format: https://username:token@github.com
#
# IMPORTANT:
# 1. Copy this file to git-credentials
# 2. Replace placeholders with actual credentials
# 3. DO NOT commit git-credentials to version control
# 4. This file is mounted at /root/.git-credentials
# ==============================================================================

# GitHub (Personal Access Token)
https://YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME:ghp_YOUR_GITHUB_TOKEN@github.com

# GitLab (Personal Access Token)
https://YOUR_GITLAB_USERNAME:glpat-YOUR_GITLAB_TOKEN@gitlab.com

# Bitbucket (App Password)
https://YOUR_BITBUCKET_USERNAME:YOUR_APP_PASSWORD@bitbucket.org

# Azure DevOps (PAT)
https://YOUR_USERNAME:YOUR_AZURE_DEVOPS_PAT@dev.azure.com

# ==============================================================================
# NOTES
# ==============================================================================
# Token Scopes Required:
# - GitHub: repo (full control), workflow, read:org
# - GitLab: api, read_repository, write_repository
# - Bitbucket: repository:write
# - Azure DevOps: Code (Full)
#
# Security Best Practices:
# - Use tokens with minimum required scopes
# - Rotate tokens regularly (every 90 days)
# - Use different tokens for different environments
# - Monitor token usage and revoke if compromised
# - Store tokens in secrets manager (Infisical, Vault) in production
# ==============================================================================
